  "question": {
    "text": "A spaceship orbits around a planet at a height of <math><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from its surface. Assuming that only gravitational field of the planet acts on the spaceship, what will be the number of complete revolutions made by the spaceship in <math><mn>24</mn></math> hours around the planet?<br />[Given: Mass of planet <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>22</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ,<br />Radius of planet <math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math><br />Gravitational constant <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> ]"
